post.description:
Checks whether a recording is the voice of an enrolled speaker. Send a recording of 3-60 seconds with at least 2 seconds of speech. The result has a `decision` (`match` or `no_match`), a `similarity` from -1 to 1 (higher means more alike) and the `threshold` used for the decision. Main failures: unknown speaker (404), too short or too little speech (422), not enough credits (402). Requires scope `speakers:verify`.

With `detect_deepfake=true` the same recording is also checked for AI-generated speech (needs scope `deepfake:detect`; that check needs a recording longer than 4 seconds, otherwise only it fails). The two checks are counted separately, and only completed checks use credits:
* if the synthetic-speech check fails, you still get the verification, with `deepfake.error`;
* if the verification fails but the synthetic-speech check completed, you get the verification's error together with `partial` (the synthetic-speech result);
* if both fail, you get the error and no credits are used.

A retry with the same `Idempotency-Key` returns the same outcome again without running or counting the checks twice.
